# Anchored to the repo root deliberately -- an earlier un-anchored `data/`
# here matched (and gitignored) infra/azure/modules/data/ too, silently
# masking that whole Terraform module from git (#47). The anchor also means
# the CLI's packaged release compose file (#280) needs no un-ignore rules,
# but they stay as a guard should the anchor ever be loosened again.
/data/
!services/inh-cli/src/inh_cli/data/
!services/inh-cli/src/inh_cli/data/docker-compose.release.yml
uploads/
playwright-report/
test-results/
eval-report.json
ingestion-benchmark-report.json
search-benchmark-report.json
.DS_Store

graphify-out/

# MkDocs build output
site/
.memory/

# Terraform working dirs (any root/module) — state and providers never belong in git.
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
